-- Periodization pass (2026-08-25). Owner: "consult the corpus, if there
-- isn't information there, send a wave to comb through the transcripts.
-- Lets get this right." The corpus DID carry periodization material, but
-- all of it incidental -- harvested for the sport-prep and accessory
-- passes, never collected to answer "what phases exist and how long does
-- each run". So: a title-routed sweep over 27 videos (Flow High
-- Performance's periodization series, Israetel's mesocycle design,
-- Juggernaut's peaking blocks, Westside conjugate, 3DMJ, Data Driven
-- Strength, Biolayne DUP) read by seven analysts against
-- brief-periodization.md.
--
-- The headline result, and the reason this pass changed a UI decision:
-- the accumulation/intensification/realization taxonomy is REAL and
-- carries distinct volume/intensity prescriptions for strength and
-- performance goals -- but multiple strong findings hold that it does
-- NOT transfer to hypertrophy, which has no performance peak to aim at
-- and whose block-to-block variation is reactive management rather than
-- planned phases. A phase strip is therefore goal-conditional, not
-- universal. Mesocycle structure (3-5 overload weeks closing in a
-- deload) IS universal and is what hypertrophy blocks show instead.

